1. PRIMARY OBJECTIVE

Build PINPOINT as a fully functional, secure, responsive application for Android, iOS where supported, and web.

The central idea is extremely simple:

Open PINPOINT → Create a Crowd or Join a Crowd → Enter a Display Name → Start Sharing Location → Chat and Track Everyone Together.

Do not require Google sign-in, Google accounts, compulsory email registration, phone-number registration, or lengthy onboarding.

Users should be able to use the application immediately.

The application must support:

- Instant crowd creation.
- Instant joining through an invitation link.
- Live GPS location sharing between all crowd members.
- Background location tracking.
- Manual STOP SHARING control.
- Shared crowd chat.
- @mentions.
- Geofencing and boundary alerts.
- Custom radius from 10 metres to 100 kilometres.
- Nearby businesses and places using Leaflet.js and OpenStreetMap.
- Paid business promotions.
- Business advertising dashboard.
- Payment integration using Razorpay where available and approved.
- Crowd deletion and complete crowd-data cleanup.

Build actual working functionality, not merely a UI prototype or simulated demonstration.

