8. GEOFENCING — CUSTOM RADIUS FROM 10 METRES TO 100 KILOMETRES

The Crowd Admin controls the geofence.

Allow any whole-number custom radius within:

- Minimum: 10 metres.
- Maximum: 100,000 metres (100 kilometres).

Do not restrict the Admin to a preset dropdown.

Provide:

- Numeric input.
- Adjustable slider.
- Clear metre/kilometre formatting.
- Validation.
- Save button.
- Current configured radius display.

Examples:

- 10 m
- 25 m
- 100 m
- 250 m
- 750 m
- 1 km
- 2.5 km
- 10 km
- 25 km
- 50 km
- 100 km

Allow the Admin to choose the geofence centre:

- Current Admin location.
- Manually selected point on the map.
- Repositioned map marker.

The Admin can modify the radius whenever required.

Boundary events

When a member crosses outside the configured radius:

1. Notify the Admin.
2. Notify the member who crossed.
3. Notify other members only if they enabled boundary notifications.

When a member returns inside:

- Notify the Admin.
- Notify the affected member.
- Notify opted-in members.

Alert information:

- Member display name.
- Inside/outside status.
- Distance from boundary centre.
- Event time.
- Current location freshness.

Prevent repeated alerts caused by GPS jitter.

Use location accuracy, distance smoothing, sensible hysteresis and event deduplication.

Geofence processing must work server-side or through a reliable native location-processing architecture. Do not rely exclusively on a web page remaining open.

